[05/12 11:24:26    763s]   timing_derate_dynamic_compatibility(root)
[05/12 11:24:26    763s]                         # bool, read/write, default=true, indices={}
[05/12 11:24:26    763s]                         # This global controls how the set_timing_derate factors that are not specified using either -static or -dynamic options are applied to the delay.  When this global is set to '1' the
[05/12 11:24:26    763s]                         # behavior will be compatible with previous releases. In this mode,  the static and dynamic components will be summed before  applying derating.  With a setting of '0',  the static and
[05/12 11:24:26    763s]                         # dynamic components will be derated separately and then combined. A setting of '0' is equivalent to using separate derate assertions with  the -dynamic and -static options explicitly
[05/12 11:24:26    763s]                         # specified.
[05/12 11:24:26    763s]   timing_derate_incremental_adjust_additive_mode(root)
